# A name too long for the explorer is cut off at its edge instead of running on
# into the editor: the second row is a file whose name is 60 characters, and to
# the right of the explorer that row, which the editor has nothing on, stays empty.
# files a.txt=A
# files this_file_has_a_name_much_longer_than_the_explorer_could_ever_show.txt=B
# open a.txt
# frames 4
# pixels 8 22 223 44 223 225 230 some
# pixels 224 22 960 44 223 225 230 none
1 key b ctrl
